WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.480
Aksel, this child is yours.

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.080
How can you be so sure about this?

3
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.680
How can I be sure?

4
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.600
Tauno can't have children
and I've only had sex with you.

5
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:09.680
Shit.

6
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.360
Shit.

7
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:12.800
Shit.

8
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.440
Can you...

9
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:18.960
Somehow...

10
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.400
Can you...

11
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.360
Well, maybe you can...

12
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.880
Get it out of your system?

13
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.760
What system?

14
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.200
I'm going to be a mom.

15
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.600
This is my chance to become a mother.

16
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.520
Nobody can know about this.
Promise me.

17
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.440
If anyone finds out...

18
00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.720
I'll have to move to the moon
if Tauno finds out.

19
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.600
But Tauno also wants children.

20
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.080
Not my child.
Not his best friend's child.

21
00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.360
Especially one made
on the floor of his living room.

22
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.360
Aksel!

23
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.680
DIVORCE IN PEACE

24
00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.960
These are really beautiful.

25
00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.200
You think?
- Yeah, I'd like that.

26
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.240
I don't know...

27
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.560
Can you imagine...

28
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:25.600
I was supposed to become
a jewellery designer, not a baker.

29
00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.120
Did I sell myself short?

30
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.040
Yeah...
- Totally, right?

31
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.200
I exchanged gold and silver
for dough.

32
00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.760
I sold myself really short.
- Buy yourself back.

33
00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.600
Start making jewellery again.

34
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.400
I don't know
if I have the strength anymore.

35
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.080
This has to be done with passion.

36
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.240
But you have enough passion.

37
00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.920
I'm so glad we can talk again.

38
00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.920
Divorce suits you, madam.

39
00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.640
But we need to support your dad.

40
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.680
He has problems
with work and all that.

41
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.120
And I can see
that he's really trying.

42
00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.160
He is actually an honest
and dutiful person.

43
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.200
Yeah.
- Yes, he really is.

44
00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.520
And that mess
with the flute player...

45
00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.680
It was just a mistake
because your dad is quite attractive.

46
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.200
And my mind is occupied with work.
- With dough.

47
00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.480
Exactly.

48
00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.720
I was neck-deep in dough.

49
00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.040
That's how mistakes happen.

50
00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.120
But I do believe
that he hasn't cheated on me.

51
00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.280
Never.

52
00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.840
Aksel.

53
00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:46.280
This is a mess.
This is a big mess.

54
00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.680
What am I supposed to do?

55
00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.920
I'm just saying that you'll be a dad.
I thought you should know that.

56
00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.280
I can't let this get out.
Tauno will kill me.

57
00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.160
But you're friends.
- That's why he'll kill me.

58
00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.960
No, Tauno has...

59
00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.720
He'll be glad...
It's better than adopting.

60
00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:08.600
He'd get another man's baby anyway,
but at least it's mine.

61
00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.760
This is insanity.

62
00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.720
It's not insane, it's my chance.

63
00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.440
Please don't say it's mine, then.

64
00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:14.880
What should I say?

65
00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.760
That I went around town?

66
00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.880
No, tell him you used a donor.
That you wanted to surprise him.

67
00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.040
Tauno already surprised me
with that adoption talk.

68
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.760
That's good.
Now it's your turn.

69
00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:28.040
You used a donor instead of...
- What?

70
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.520
I don't know.

71
00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.040
You have to figure out
how to hide this or...

72
00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.120
I don't know.

73
00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.960
At least before the kid starts
playing violin and has my face.

74
00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:41.360
Tauno would like the child more
if it had your face.

75
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.760
He would start
hating the child because

76
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.280
it would remind him of the cheating.

77
00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:51.400
You have to tell him
you used a sperm donor.

78
00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.200
What do I tell him?

79
00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.560
That I got a jar of sperm in town

80
00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.760
and poured it inside of me?

81
00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.480
And <i>voilà</i> ?

82
00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.480
Tauno will know something's off.
- No, he won't.

83
00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.680
It'll work.

84
00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.280
Tauno doesn't know
how these things work

85
00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.800
because it doesn't concern
the Defence League or hunting bears.

86
00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:16.680
I don't know...
- What don't you know?

87
00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.880
You have to promise me
you won't drag me into this mess.

88
00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:26.480
This mess?
- You know what I mean.

89
00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.760
Please don't say it was me.

90
00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.280
Mirjam.

91
00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.200
Mirjam.

92
00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.600
Mirjam. Mirjam!

93
00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.520
Please promise me.

94
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.520
I'm not promising anything.

95
00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.400
Mirjam, you have to promise
you won't say anything to Tauno.

96
00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.440
Secrets...

97
00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.400
I accept that Aksel has secrets.

98
00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.160
What secrets?

99
00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.800
Everyone has small quirks

100
00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:57.000
or things that they
don't want to talk about.

101
00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.520
For example,
I always knock when entering.

102
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.880
I don't understand.
- What?

103
00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.760
I know that you're superstitious,

104
00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.880
even though you
constantly talk about facts

105
00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.200
and how democratic
countries distort facts.

106
00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.520
But they do!

107
00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.320
There is no such thing as democracy.

108
00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.880
Yet on the inside, you're superstitious.

109
00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.440
What are you talking about...

110
00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.400
For example, you spit three times
over your shoulder.

111
00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.400
Nonsense!
- Quietly, like this...

112
00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.960
Small rituals like that.
You're basically a believer.

113
00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.480
But I believe in science.

114
00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.240
What are you talking about?
I'm not...

115
00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.000
Yes, you are.
You live in a different time.

116
00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.400
Everything modern gets
on your nerves.

117
00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.680
I think that deep inside,
you support the Jihad.

118
00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.640
That's your biggest secret.

119
00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:41.600
Your story is completely distorted.
- And tilted.

120
00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:45.520
This talk is distorted
and is completely not true.

121
00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:47.960
The fact that I have enough sense

122
00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:53.160
to stand against liberal brainwashing
does not make me old-fashioned.

123
00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.240
You resist current
and normal brainwashing,

124
00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.160
but gladly enjoy
medieval brainwashing

125
00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.480
where women are beneath you

126
00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.600
and everything foreign belongs
automatically on the stake.

127
00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.360
What are you talking about?
How did we end up here?

128
00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.160
We've reached secrets.

129
00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:15.960
We've reached the sixth task,
which is...

130
00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:18.800
'The well of secrets.'

131
00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.240
The task entails

132
00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.440
for you to arrange
a cosy evening at home...

133
00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.840
A spiritual one...
- See!

134
00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.280
What?

135
00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.360
Is 'spiritual' a modern
or medieval word?

136
00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.320
Did I misunderstand something?

137
00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.440
Which way am I being brainwashed now?

138
00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.440
You'll sit down, hold hands
and look at each other.

139
00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:42.520
Then, you'll reveal
what you've been holding in.

140
00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.520
You mean like a deceit?

141
00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:46.960
It doesn't have to be
a deceit, but...

142
00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.960
In the name of honesty,
it should be something important.

143
00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.760
A substantial secret,

144
00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.840
which you can release
into the universe together.

145
00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.960
To cancel, to let loose.

146
00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:00.760
I've always said everything out loud.

147
00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:03.360
I don't have any secrets.

148
00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.960
Think about it.
- Alright...

149
00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.160
There's no point
in bringing old baggage

150
00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.080
into a new relationship.

151
00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:24.560
Hello?

152
00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:26.960
Yes, I'm listening.

153
00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:29.840
Okay.

154
00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:32.480
Yeah.

155
00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.120
Of course!

156
00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.400
Alright.
Thank you very much!

157
00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.960
Yeah, see you. Bye!

158
00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:48.560
What happened?
- Yes!

159
00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.240
Like they say.

160
00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.440
Do they say that?

161
00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:54.760
I got an audition to ERSO.

162
00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.160
A friend arranged everything.

163
00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.680
I can kick-start
my career as a musician again.

164
00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.360
What about your stage fright?
- Stage fright...

165
00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.800
It's only up here.

166
00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.920
I know now what I'm worth.

167
00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.720
I'll just step on the stage

168
00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:10.360
and let the music flow.

169
00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.200
Congratulations.

170
00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.960
Big stages await me. Son!

171
00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.400
Your mom will soon see
who she's messing with!

172
00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.520
Aksel.
- Yeah?

173
00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.840
Come here.
- What's up?

174
00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.480
Come on.

175
00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:37.640
Have a seat.

176
00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.320
Sit down.
- Did something happen?

177
00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.280
What's up?

178
00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:52.440
You know.

179
00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.480
What do I know?

180
00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.880
You know what's going on.

181
00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.920
The child.

182
00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:02.920
Tauno, honestly, I'm so sorry...

183
00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:04.880
It's like I've been
hit over the head.

184
00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.520
We need to talk.
- That's what I'm saying.

185
00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:13.160
I can only blame myself for this.

186
00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:16.440
You? No, I'm blaming myself.

187
00:09:16.440 --> 00:09:19.640
Why didn't I think
about adoption sooner?

188
00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:23.480
Why did I let things go so far that
Mirjam would start doubting me?

189
00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:27.600
That? Yes, that...
- Now you have it.

190
00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:30.400
Now I'm going back and forth
between feeling sad and happy.

191
00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:32.160
Emotions.
- Emotions?

192
00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.960
Exactly.
- We need to celebrate.

193
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.200
Really?
- Celebrate like we used to.

194
00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:39.480
I have to understand
that I should be happy.

195
00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:40.920
I have to...

196
00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.440
Come to ours in the evening.

197
00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.840
A surprise dinner.
- Of course, we'll come.

198
00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:47.600
We'll surprise Mirjam.

199
00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:49.880
Sit like we used to.
No crap.

200
00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:51.760
Only joy and jokes.

201
00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:55.440
Have a laugh,
see the joy in life.

202
00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.400
And the kid...

203
00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.240
This could be good for you two, too.

204
00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.480
How?
- What do you mean how?

205
00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:05.320
Maybe you should expand the family.

206
00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.960
No...
- Do your parts still work?

207
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.160
Well, now...
- Still blasting?

208
00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:14.680
We'll have a drink,
some good food and then blast off.

209
00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:17.960
Seven o'clock.
Decided.

210
00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.840
Take your thing with you.

211
00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:37.040
The violin.
You'll play for Mirjam.

212
00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:52.440
Come on, come on, come on!

213
00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.360
Very good.

214
00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:59.360
We can discuss with you,
experienced parents,

215
00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.040
where the nursery should be
and all that.

216
00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:05.680
Wow, you're so excited.
- Yes, I am.

217
00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:09.880
Tauno will be such a great dad.
- Of course.

218
00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:12.160
Come now.
Quietly.

219
00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:19.200
What's going on?

220
00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.680
Such wonderful news
that you two are going to be parents.

221
00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:27.240
That was the missing
mystical piece of joy - a child.

222
00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.960
Congratulations on the decision.

223
00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:33.600
Thank you.

224
00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.400
It's a teddy bear.

225
00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:37.640
It'll suit both, girl or boy.

226
00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:40.520
Really?

227
00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:43.800
Congratulations.
- Are you being serious?

228
00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.880
Who will you take?
A boy or a girl?

229
00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.680
Well, there are only two options.

230
00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.480
I've only talked
with them on the phone.

231
00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:55.240
This all takes time.

232
00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:56.960
It's a long process.

233
00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:59.880
But we're okay.

234
00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.680
Our age is good.

235
00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:03.480
And we have a lot of money.

236
00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:04.760
So cool.

237
00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:09.640
If we manage to get a really tiny one,
then we can name it ourselves, too.

238
00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:13.160
If we get a boy,

239
00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:16.440
then I thought we should name him

240
00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:18.760
Aksel.

241
00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:24.240
We will have a teeny-tiny Aksel.

242
00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:25.680
That's really sweet of you.

243
00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.400
We're still discussing it.

244
00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.240
If it's a girl,

245
00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:32.960
then I thought her name should be

246
00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:35.000
Rain.

247
00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.440
So that's that.

248
00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:45.720
Yeah, so...

249
00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:50.560
Let's drink in honour of a new life,
a new dad, a new mom,

250
00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.480
and everything else new.

251
00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:56.720
Cheers.
- Cheers to the two of you!

252
00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:01.480
You have to drink every single drop.

253
00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.200
What's wrong? Drink up!

254
00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.960
It's not like you're having the baby.

255
00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:15.240
Come on, chug it all down!

256
00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:18.280
I don't want to on an empty stomach.
Can you put on some music?

257
00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.640
Music, right.

258
00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.680
Aksel, can you help
me chop some carrots?

259
00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:24.240
Soon, we'll only have
children's songs on.

260
00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.760
It's high time to rock on and drink.

261
00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:29.440
It's not that bad.

262
00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:32.600
Actually...

263
00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:35.760
Actually, I'll give
up all of my bad habits.

264
00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:37.080
I'll be a new man.

265
00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.680
For the child.

266
00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.960
Of course.
You'll be a great dad.

267
00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:44.960
Mirjam, for God's sake.

268
00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:48.160
You have to understand me.
- I will if you don't tell him.

269
00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:50.360
This may be my only chance.

270
00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:54.360
You will kill me,
you will kill us both if Tauno...

271
00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:56.280
Don't be overly dramatic.

272
00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:58.800
God, why is this happening to me?

273
00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:01.080
You? It's because we had sex.
- Quiet!

274
00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:04.160
What?
- I was being rhetorical.

275
00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:07.880
If we'd had rhetorical sex,
I'd be rhetorically pregnant.

276
00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.440
But I am pregnant for real.

277
00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:13.160
It was real sex with sweat,
skin and passion.

278
00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.400
Please be quiet.

279
00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:18.880
I can't lie to Tauno.
I just can't do that to him.

280
00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:21.400
Please, be quiet.
- I can't even look him in the eye.

281
00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:23.960
Please, Mirjam. For God's sake.

282
00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.640
This doesn't oblige you to anything.

283
00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:28.160
I don't need child support
or anything else from you.

284
00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:30.520
Yes, but coming clean...

285
00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:35.040
I just can't lie to him.
I'm not that kind of person.

286
00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:36.760
You can have sex but not lie?

287
00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:39.040
These are completely different things!
- How?

288
00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:40.960
Which one is worse?

289
00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:42.680
Which one is worse?

290
00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:46.560
We're wondering whether
Tabasco or adjika is worse.

291
00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:48.480
I'd take adjika any time.

292
00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.840
Adjika would be
a good name for a daughter.

293
00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:54.560
It's sauna time!
It's already 150° C. Come on!

294
00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:58.760
We have to figure out...
- I'm not promising anything.

295
00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.320
It's cooling down.
Come on!

296
00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.080
Wait...

297
00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:07.000
How much did you throw?

298
00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.520
It would be nice to
crawl around with a boy.

299
00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:17.280
Fool around.

300
00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.800
As soon as his finger
could pull a trigger,

301
00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:23.120
we'd start shooting.

302
00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:26.280
But a girl...

303
00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:28.520
A girl is cuter.

304
00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:33.880
Which one would you like to have
if you were expecting?

305
00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:36.880
I'm not sure...

306
00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:40.680
A man and a cat are drinking vodka...

307
00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:43.640
The man starts complaining

308
00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.480
that his wife is
pregnant with triplets.

309
00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:48.160
'What will happen now?'

310
00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:50.680
'The house is small,
we need to buy a new one.'

311
00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:54.160
'The salary is small,
I need to take on multiple jobs.'

312
00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.200
'Everything is screwed.'

313
00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.720
Then the cat says:

314
00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:59.480
'Don't worry about it.'

315
00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:03.520
'Put an ad in the newspaper
and you'll be rid of her.'

316
00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:11.200
If we're going to separate,
we might as well be honest.

317
00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.600
Yeah, get rid of our hearts, too.

318
00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:15.680
You need to make space in your heart

319
00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:18.640
or soon there'll be a notice
that it's too full.

320
00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.360
Yeah...

321
00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:23.520
The heart is an admirable organ.

322
00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:27.320
So, our hands are...

323
00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:30.240
You go first.

324
00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.960
You sure you don't want to go first?

325
00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:38.200
Well, this therapy was your idea,
so you go on...

326
00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.240
Okay.

327
00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:41.000
So...

328
00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:43.120
A secret.

329
00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:48.440
A secret that I've kept
all these years.

330
00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:50.560
Well...

331
00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:52.040
I thought about it

332
00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.640
and thought about it some more.

333
00:16:55.560 --> 00:17:00.760
You remember that
I was in a relationship when we met?

334
00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:04.400
Yeah, with your coursemate.
That jewellery designer.

335
00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.080
Valdek.
- Yeah, him.

336
00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:08.400
I was supposed to...

337
00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.880
You and I had just met.

338
00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:12.960
Sparks started flying between us.

339
00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:18.840
I had to go and visit
Valdek for the last time...

340
00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:22.120
To end it in a civil way.
- Yeah.

341
00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:24.280
And...

342
00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:26.560
We got into an argument.

343
00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:29.240
He started acting really childishly

344
00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:32.600
and tried to get me
into bed one last time.

345
00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:34.920
God...
- No, no, no, no.

346
00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:37.200
I didn't, but...

347
00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.120
But he was very insistent.

348
00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:41.840
He was so sad,

349
00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:44.560
but also very excited.

350
00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:46.600
So, as a goodbye,

351
00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:51.520
I quickly finished him off
with my hand one last time.

352
00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.400
Yeah...

353
00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:55.120
It was quite disgusting.

354
00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:57.440
I didn't feel anything.

355
00:17:57.440 --> 00:17:59.720
Valdek cried the entire time.

356
00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:01.600
But...

357
00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:08.160
There wasn't any 'Me Too' back then

358
00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:10.440
and I though it was
a way to say goodbye,

359
00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:13.480
to comfort and calm him down.

360
00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:14.640
And...

361
00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:19.520
And I also felt that I had
been very unjust towards him.

362
00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:22.400
Of course...

363
00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:25.000
It didn't mean anything.

364
00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:27.440
Technically, we were
still in a relationship.

365
00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:29.240
Technically, yes.

366
00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:35.200
Your turn.

367
00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:39.840
Well...

368
00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.520
I thought about it...

369
00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:46.680
And thought about it.

370
00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:50.640
And...

371
00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.960
Remember when we were on holiday?

372
00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.240
At Pühajärv with the kids.

373
00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:02.520
That young swimming coach?

374
00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:04.720
That Baywatch babe?

375
00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.200
What?

376
00:19:06.440 --> 00:19:08.720
I don't know what
you're talking about.

377
00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:10.160
Okay.

378
00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:14.960
We had that small
gathering at the campsite.

379
00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:17.960
I guess you don't remember.

380
00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:21.040
You left half of that
blueberry cake uneaten.

381
00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.640
Said you would have it for breakfast.

382
00:19:24.520 --> 00:19:25.760
No, I don't remember.

383
00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:29.000
Anyway, I took it

384
00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.280
and put it away

385
00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:34.080
so you could have it for breakfast.
But during the night...

386
00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:37.600
I woke up and ate all of the cake.

387
00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:40.360
In the morning...

388
00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:45.400
You asked where the blueberry
cake was and I said I didn't know.

389
00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:49.920
Somebody probably ate it.
One of the other guests.

390
00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:51.240
Maybe the kids.

391
00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:55.240
A half-eaten cake?

392
00:19:55.280 --> 00:19:58.160
That's so pointless,
I don't even remember that.

393
00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:02.200
But it's been a burden
for me all those years.

394
00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:04.440
Poor you...

395
00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:10.080
You're sure you don't have anything
bigger and more serious to tell me?

396
00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.560
What?

397
00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:13.080
I don't know.

398
00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:16.800
That you were a woman
before meeting me.

399
00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:20.960
Or that you have
a secret child somewhere.

400
00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:22.240
A secret child...

401
00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:27.560
There's no secret child.
Where would it be?

402
00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:33.040
Alright.

403
00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:38.520
I will let go of that blueberry
cake that I don't even remember.

404
00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:42.480
Universe, take that cake
and eat it all.

405
00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:49.680
And you'll let that Valdek thing go.
- Yeah.

406
00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:54.960
Universe, take Valdek...

407
00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:56.560
and that...

408
00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:00.840
technical goodbye handy.

409
00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:05.320
Take Valdek and place him
into the darkest possible hole.

410
00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:07.480
Thank you, Universe.

411
00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:13.720
Can you feel it?

412
00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:19.600
It's the first time we've
accomplished a therapy task.

413
00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.160
Yeah.

414
00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.840
Seems like the universe
wants us to get a divorce.

415
00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:29.840
Morning.
- Morning.

416
00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:34.120
Are you going to school?
- Yeah and I'm in a rush.

417
00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:36.320
How is that project going?

418
00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:40.920
What project?

419
00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:45.840
You said you had to present
something visual to a committee.

420
00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:47.640
Right.

421
00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:49.360
That's going well.

422
00:21:49.640 --> 00:21:51.400
Good to hear.

423
00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:53.400
How is that jewellery
business going?

424
00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:54.800
Well, that...

425
00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:57.160
I'm meeting up with
a gallery owner.

426
00:21:57.160 --> 00:22:01.400
I want to see whether I'd have
any market as a jewellery designer.

427
00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:03.320
Looking at the lay of the land.

428
00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:04.920
Morning.
- Morning.

429
00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:06.640
How are you, dad?

430
00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:09.720
Me? I have that audition.

431
00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:14.120
I've basically been accepted to ERSO,
so it's just formalities.

432
00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:15.960
Good luck, then.

433
00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:18.520
Really?

434
00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:21.120
Yeah, what...

435
00:22:36.560 --> 00:22:37.760
Valdek.

436
00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:40.600
You're running this gallery?

437
00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:44.360
It was supposed to be Eda.

438
00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:46.040
Eda...

439
00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:48.880
Eda doesn't work here anymore.

440
00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:51.440
Since yesterday, actually.

441
00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:54.960
She's moving to Türi.

442
00:22:56.280 --> 00:22:57.840
She found someone there.

443
00:22:58.040 --> 00:22:59.280
Look at that...

444
00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:03.040
Well, I guess that's that.

445
00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:05.760
Hello, Valdek.
- Hello.

446
00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:18.400
Haven't seen you...

447
00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:20.520
...in so many years.

448
00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:24.560
And now, here...

449
00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:30.640
Great.

450
00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:33.960
That...

451
00:23:35.320 --> 00:23:38.920
Our breakup was...

452
00:23:41.040 --> 00:23:42.400
...pretty crazy.

453
00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:45.880
What's the point in
bringing that up now?

454
00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:46.920
Yeah...

455
00:23:48.520 --> 00:23:51.280
I heard that...

456
00:23:51.520 --> 00:23:52.920
...you're getting a divorce.

457
00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.960
From that...

458
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:57.680
That man you had...

459
00:23:59.480 --> 00:24:01.520
That trombone player.
- Aksel.

460
00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:03.120
The violin player.

461
00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:04.560
But yes, it's true.

462
00:24:05.840 --> 00:24:07.880
Where did you hear that?
- Well...

463
00:24:08.520 --> 00:24:10.240
From the Artists' Association.

464
00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:16.560
Somebody said it
was talked about online.

465
00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:19.680
Yeah, I guess the internet
is everywhere nowadays.

466
00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:22.280
Yeah, so...

467
00:24:23.640 --> 00:24:25.760
It's true?
- Yeah.

468
00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:27.880
It's the end of one life stage.

469
00:24:27.960 --> 00:24:29.520
Yeah...

470
00:24:32.240 --> 00:24:36.160
One stage seems to have
been left unfinished...

471
00:24:36.200 --> 00:24:39.920
Yeah, well...
If we're being serious for a second,

472
00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:43.720
what do you think, Valdek?
Should I show you my sketches?

473
00:24:48.640 --> 00:24:50.160
Yes.

474
00:24:52.360 --> 00:24:54.880
Let's have a look.

475
00:24:58.120 --> 00:24:59.240
Let's have a look.

476
00:25:06.080 --> 00:25:07.200
Aksel.

477
00:25:07.960 --> 00:25:10.200
Aksel.
- Yeah?

478
00:25:11.080 --> 00:25:13.280
What happened?
- What happened...

479
00:25:13.600 --> 00:25:15.840
I got an audition.

480
00:25:16.640 --> 00:25:18.200
I went on stage and...

481
00:25:19.640 --> 00:25:23.240
Everything went on
from where it was left off.

482
00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:26.760
I started playing and suddenly
felt everything start to spin,

483
00:25:26.760 --> 00:25:28.320
my mouth went dry,

484
00:25:28.360 --> 00:25:31.040
my legs went heavy,
my stomach went hollow.

485
00:25:31.280 --> 00:25:32.920
Stage fright again.

486
00:25:34.160 --> 00:25:36.880
That big ass stage fright is back.

487
00:25:38.080 --> 00:25:41.480
I'm completely useless.
- You're wrong.

488
00:25:41.600 --> 00:25:43.800
We'll get over it.

489
00:25:43.840 --> 00:25:44.920
Listen to me.

490
00:25:45.120 --> 00:25:47.720
I know how you'll beat this fright.

491
00:25:47.720 --> 00:25:49.440
You need to man up.

492
00:25:49.840 --> 00:25:52.520
You're going to come hunting with me.

493
00:25:52.680 --> 00:25:54.320
You need to...

494
00:25:54.720 --> 00:25:58.320
kill a deer.
Then, you'll be a man.

495
00:25:58.400 --> 00:26:01.480
Then, you'll go on that stage
and laugh at your fright.

496
00:26:01.520 --> 00:26:04.560
Thanks, Tauno, but...
- Look at that.

497
00:26:05.400 --> 00:26:07.760
What's Mirjam doing here?

498
00:26:07.800 --> 00:26:09.520
The ladies wanted
to discuss something.

499
00:26:09.560 --> 00:26:12.640
Mirjam wanted to have
a heart to heart with Laura.

500
00:26:14.680 --> 00:26:15.880
Something about kids.

501
00:26:15.920 --> 00:26:19.280
What about?
- Ladies and their secrets.

502
00:26:19.800 --> 00:26:22.960
I'll get the wheels spinning, okay?

503
00:26:23.360 --> 00:26:26.280
Let's go to the woods
and you'll shoot a bear.

504
00:26:26.360 --> 00:26:28.560
And become a man.
- Yeah, I need to go...

505
00:26:30.400 --> 00:26:32.800
Aksel, it's decided, right?

506
00:26:32.920 --> 00:26:34.400
The two of us in the woods?

507
00:26:34.960 --> 00:26:36.000
Shooting a bear.

508
00:26:36.680 --> 00:26:37.680
Amazing!

509
00:26:37.720 --> 00:26:41.880
If you need help or anything,
please let me know.

510
00:26:41.960 --> 00:26:46.520
I'll show you how to wrap
and we can talk about all that.

511
00:26:46.640 --> 00:26:47.920
Yes, thank you.

512
00:26:50.080 --> 00:26:51.160
So...

513
00:26:51.520 --> 00:26:54.360
You didn't want to use a donor?

514
00:26:56.240 --> 00:26:59.280
The thing with that is...
Well, Aksel...

515
00:27:02.320 --> 00:27:04.600
Hello.
Look who's here!

516
00:27:06.960 --> 00:27:08.080
How was it?

517
00:27:08.760 --> 00:27:09.800
At the gallery?

518
00:27:11.600 --> 00:27:14.320
Yeah... Well... Yeah...

519
00:27:14.360 --> 00:27:17.240
Turns out, an old
acquaintance of mine runs it

520
00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:21.160
and he asked to see my sketches,
so maybe it'll work out.

521
00:27:22.080 --> 00:27:23.600
How about you?

522
00:27:26.120 --> 00:27:27.200
Yeah...

523
00:27:27.840 --> 00:27:29.760
Could we talk about this privately?

524
00:27:31.960 --> 00:27:32.960
Of course.

525
00:27:41.240 --> 00:27:42.800
Well?

526
00:27:43.800 --> 00:27:45.320
My stage fright is back.

527
00:27:46.440 --> 00:27:48.400
I was like a statue on stage.

528
00:27:49.960 --> 00:27:50.960
Damn.

529
00:27:51.840 --> 00:27:52.840
That's sad.

530
00:27:53.200 --> 00:27:55.680
Maybe it's for the best.
I'm going hunting with Tauno.

531
00:27:55.920 --> 00:27:58.080
What?
- I'm going hunting with Tauno.

532
00:27:59.320 --> 00:28:00.320
You?

533
00:28:00.440 --> 00:28:01.440
Yes.

534
00:28:01.880 --> 00:28:02.960
For real?

535
00:28:02.960 --> 00:28:04.080
Yes.

536
00:28:04.200 --> 00:28:05.760
Maybe that's what I need.

537
00:28:06.760 --> 00:28:08.240
To get over the fright.

538
00:28:09.480 --> 00:28:11.200
Do something unprecedented.

539
00:28:12.480 --> 00:28:13.520
Great.

540
00:28:14.880 --> 00:28:16.760
At least something manly.

541
00:28:18.360 --> 00:28:20.280
Something primal.

542
00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:27.640
<i>RIHARD</i>

543
00:28:37.240 --> 00:28:38.360
Yes?

544
00:28:38.560 --> 00:28:41.360
<i>Good evening, Laura.</i>
I hope it's not too late...

545
00:28:43.080 --> 00:28:44.760
No, no.

546
00:28:44.840 --> 00:28:46.040
Not at all.

547
00:28:46.200 --> 00:28:49.960
<i>I wanted to discuss with you</i>
something about the restaurant.

548
00:28:51.440 --> 00:28:54.240
Well, if there is any use of me.

549
00:28:54.400 --> 00:28:57.080
<i>I feel like I can't do anything</i>
without you anymore.

550
00:28:58.200 --> 00:28:59.920
Guess what, baby.

551
00:29:00.800 --> 00:29:02.440
Two million.

552
00:29:12.880 --> 00:29:13.880
Tauno.

553
00:29:14.680 --> 00:29:16.360
Tauno, I can't.

554
00:29:18.400 --> 00:29:21.200
Everything's alright.
We'll go there tomorrow at 11.

555
00:29:21.400 --> 00:29:22.800
Everything's been agreed on.

556
00:29:22.840 --> 00:29:25.880
The adoption process may begin.

557
00:29:26.200 --> 00:29:27.520
It's not about that.

558
00:29:27.560 --> 00:29:29.280
Tauno, I can't anymore.

559
00:29:30.760 --> 00:29:31.760
What's up?
